    "result_text": "The full test suite is green. Here's a summary of what I implemented.\n\n## What changed\n\nThe spec: when a create request sets `sharesHousehold: true`, allow an owner at an address already used by a same-last-name owner, give every member of that household the same stable `householdId`, and return it. The controller already skipped the duplicate check for this flag; the missing piece was assigning and returning the shared identifier.\n\n**New logic, each in its own small unit:**\n\n- **`HouseholdKey`** (util) \u2014 the single definition of household identity: normalized `lastName + address` as a comparison key, plus `idFor(key)` producing a deterministic, stable 12-char id (SHA-256 prefix). Both the existing uniqueness check and the new assignment reuse it, so their matching can't drift apart.\n- **`OwnerHouseholdRegistrar`** (`@Component`) \u2014 on opt-in, finds existing owners in the same household, shares one `householdId` across them (reusing an existing member's id, else deriving the stable one), backfills members that lack it, and stamps the joining owner. If no household exists yet, it does nothing.\n- **`OwnerHouseholdUniquenessValidator`** \u2014 refactored to use `HouseholdKey`, dropping its private duplicate of the normalization logic.\n\n**Wiring / plumbing:**\n- `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` now calls the registrar in the `sharesHousehold=true` branch (the `else` of the existing uniqueness check).\n- `Owner` entity gained a persisted `householdId` (`household_id` column, added to all four schema dialects \u2014 hsqldb/h2/mysql/postgres).\n- `openapi.yml` gained a read-only `householdId` property on the `Owner` response schema; the generated `OwnerDto` field and MapStruct mapping flow through automatically.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreJoinersShareHouseholdId` passes: two owners joining an existing household receive the same non-blank `householdId`. `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0 \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS`.",
